:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s⊥t$ and $w⊥t$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447433} :answer-field/id #uuid "a73fa367-9679-5d96-ac5d-85f37d715606" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1f0a9542-3ba4-5c20-945c-8b2a173ef94b" :question/math-academy-id "q-151142" :question/problem "![](images/09/0927f7a957a2a5d8b91aafd71e488ce535f2c8ada2ef97d0592d58b75cd2eece.png)\n\nFrom the diagram above, which of the following statements is true?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $a∥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are parallel, and\n\n- $a⊥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are perpendicular.\n\nIn the given diagram, there are two pairs of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $s$ is perpendicular to $t,$ which we write as $s⊥t$\n\n- $w$ is perpendicular to $t,$ which we write as $w⊥t.$\n\n![](images/75/756f579f20695c46394e6667fd78444504b1470619ea6ca4b68eed87eeed934e.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct statement is $s⊥t$ and $w⊥t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96a6d19b-af7f-5abd-9713-abb4455e52bf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel and Perpendicular Lines in Figures"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cf0cfe-7dc5-5836-a44f-5d124e0e733b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{―}{RS}⊥\\overset{―}{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447387} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4993c1-7ce8-53eb-81eb-3f96aa79fa2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{―}{TP}⊥\\overset{―}{PQ}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447396} {:answer/id #uuid "5d532c81-f440-5d55-8b5a-e9ff28e29b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921